WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.736
School Eight A begins with drug language and follows pharmacokinetics, pharmacodynamics and receptor systems. We will keep those concepts connected to one clinical question: what should this medication change in this patient?
学校8A先教药物语言，再教药动学、药效学及受体系统。这里把这些概念连到一个临床问题：这药应让眼前患者发生什么变化？

00:00:14.736 --> 00:00:26.136
A dose that is calculated correctly can still be the wrong decision. The indication, authority, route, formulation and patient physiology must all support giving it.
剂量算对，决策仍可能错。适应证、权限、途径、剂型和患者生理都必须支持给药。

00:00:26.136 --> 00:00:40.848
Nancy chapter Seven provides the principal-textbook topic connection. The school module supplies this weekend's domains; current operational sources resolve drug and scope details rather than being silently mixed with classroom examples.
Nancy第7章提供主教材主题对应。学校模块确定本周学习领域，现行操作来源用于核对药物及权限细节，不与课堂示例暗中混合。

00:00:40.848 --> 00:00:53.520
Scientific examples here do not authorize every listed drug or route for a student or a PCP. Learn the mechanism, then separately verify that you may perform the intervention in the actual setting.
这里科学示例不授权学生或PCP使用所列所有药物和途径。先学机制，再单独核实实际环境是否允许进行干预。

00:00:53.520 --> 00:01:07.272
Use the generic name to identify the medication and recognize any brand name on the package. Read the actual label every time, including formulation, strength, route, expiry and integrity.
用通用名确认药物，也认识包装商品名。每次都读真实标签，包括剂型、强度、途径、效期和完整性。

00:01:07.272 --> 00:01:19.368
A dose is the amount intended for the patient. Concentration tells you the amount in each unit of volume. Volume equals dose divided by concentration after their units have been aligned.
剂量是打算给患者的药物量；浓度表示每单位体积的量。先统一单位，再用剂量除以浓度得到体积。

00:01:19.368 --> 00:01:35.376
For a fictional calculation, six milligrams from a two-milligram-per-millilitre product requires three millilitres. If the label instead says ten milligrams per millilitre, the same six-milligram dose requires zero point six millilitres.
虚构计算：6毫克来自每毫升2毫克制剂，需要3毫升；若标签是每毫升10毫克，同样6毫克只需0.6毫升。

00:01:35.376 --> 00:01:45.792
Never identify concentration from cap colour or familiar packaging alone. A correct medication name does not rescue a tenfold concentration error.
不能只凭瓶盖颜色或熟悉包装判断浓度。药名对了，也不能抵消十倍浓度错误。

00:01:45.792 --> 00:01:58.464
An indication is the clinical reason to use a drug. It must fit the assessed patient, not just a symptom word. Wheeze, for example, does not identify every underlying cause.
适应证是使用药物的临床理由，必须符合已评估患者，不能只匹配一个症状词。例如喘鸣不能确定所有潜在病因。

00:01:58.464 --> 00:02:12.624
A contraindication and a precaution are not identical. Read the current source for the specific situation: one may preclude treatment, while the other requires a changed plan, closer assessment or consultation.
禁忌与慎用不一样。应读当前来源对具体情境的规定；前者可能阻止给药，后者可能要求改变计划、更仔细评估或会诊。

00:02:12.624 --> 00:02:26.856
Side effects may be expected but unwanted; an adverse effect is harmful. A predictable effect can still be a serious adverse effect, such as opioid respiratory depression. Expected does not mean acceptable.
副作用可能可预期但不想要；不良作用有伤害。可预期作用仍可能严重，例如阿片呼吸抑制。可预期不等于可以接受。

00:02:26.856 --> 00:02:39.648
Toxicity is not limited to deliberate overdose. An ordinary dose may become unsafe with accumulation, organ dysfunction, interacting medicines or unusual sensitivity.
毒性不只来自故意过量。常规剂量也可能因蓄积、器官功能异常、药物相互作用或特殊敏感性变得不安全。

00:02:39.648 --> 00:02:53.352
Pharmacokinetics asks what the body does to the drug. Absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion commonly overlap in time; they are not four stages that must finish one after another.
药动学问身体怎样处理药物。吸收、分布、代谢和排泄通常在时间上重叠，不是必须依次完成的四段。

00:02:53.352 --> 00:03:08.616
Intravenous administration enters systemic blood directly and bypasses an absorption step. Calling an IV dose instantly absorbed is convenient shorthand, but it hides the important difference from tissue or gut delivery.
静脉给药直接进入体循环，绕过吸收步骤。把它简称“立即吸收”虽然方便，却掩盖了与组织或胃肠给药的重要区别。

00:03:08.616 --> 00:03:21.816
Reaching blood is not the same as reaching the effect site or producing peak effect. Circulation, tissue distribution and receptor responses can still take time after an IV injection.
进入血液不等于已经到达效应部位或产生峰效。静脉注射后，循环、组织分布和受体反应仍可能需要时间。

00:03:21.816 --> 00:03:33.600
After administration, compare the expected course with the observed patient. Physiology can make a familiar drug slower, stronger or longer acting than you anticipated.
给药后比较预期过程与实际患者。生理情况可能使熟悉的药物比预想更慢、更强或更持久。

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:46.584
A muscle or subcutaneous injection must reach local circulation. Reduced tissue perfusion can delay or make absorption less predictable; that matters when interpreting a slow response.
肌肉或皮下注射必须进入局部循环。组织灌注下降可能使吸收延迟或更难预测，因此不能随意解释慢反应。

00:03:46.584 --> 00:04:00.960
The formulation also matters. A tablet must dissolve; an inhaled aerosol must reach a useful airway location; an intranasal dose needs an appropriate device, volume and mucosal contact.
剂型也重要。片剂要溶解，吸入气雾要到有效气道位置，鼻内剂量需要适当装置、体积和黏膜接触。

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:14.808
Surface area, solubility, ionization and transport influence membrane passage. Do not turn a broad rule such as lipid-soluble drugs cross easily into a claim that every tissue barrier is absolute.
表面积、溶解性、离子化和转运影响过膜。不能把“脂溶性较易通过”之类概括变成每道组织屏障都绝对的断言。

00:04:14.808 --> 00:04:28.584
A delayed response is not permission to improvise a new route or stack doses before the expected onset. Reassess physiology, delivery and the indicated repeat interval while supporting immediate threats.
反应延迟不允许临时自创新途径，也不能在预期起效前堆叠剂量。应复评生理、给药是否有效及规定重复间隔，同时支持即时威胁。

00:04:28.584 --> 00:04:42.912
Bioavailability is the fraction of a dose reaching systemic circulation unchanged. IV delivery is the reference with one hundred percent bioavailability; other routes depend on absorption and presystemic loss.
生物利用度是原形药进入体循环的剂量比例。静脉是百分之百的参照；其他途径取决于吸收及进入体循环前损失。

00:04:42.912 --> 00:04:58.680
After gut absorption, portal blood passes through the liver before systemic circulation. Metabolism in the gut wall and liver can lower oral availability. This is first-pass metabolism, not simply a synonym for slow absorption.
胃肠吸收后，门静脉血先经肝才进入体循环。肠壁及肝代谢可降低口服利用度，这叫首过代谢，不只是吸收慢的同义词。

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:15.288
In formal comparisons, absolute availability uses the non-IV area under the concentration-time curve divided by the IV area, with correction for different doses. It is not estimated just by comparing how quickly a patient reports relief.
正式比较中，绝对利用度用非静脉浓度时间曲线下面积除以静脉面积，并校正不同剂量；不是只比较患者多快说舒服了。

00:05:15.288 --> 00:05:29.928
Sublingual or nasal delivery can avoid much first-pass loss for the absorbed portion, but swallowed drug and incomplete delivery still matter. Bypassing first pass does not make different formulations dose-equivalent.
舌下或鼻内被吸收部分可避免大部分首过损失，但吞咽及不完全给药仍重要。绕过首过并不使不同剂型剂量等效。

00:05:29.928 --> 00:05:46.800
IV offers direct access and controlled administration, but needs an indicated invasive procedure. IO accesses the vascular marrow space and has specific restrictions; it is not a routine interchangeable option for every PCP patient.
静脉提供直接通路及受控给药，但侵入操作必须有适应证。骨内进入骨髓血管间隙，有专门限制，不是所有PCP患者都可常规互换。

00:05:46.800 --> 00:06:01.008
IM and SC routes depend on tissue absorption and the product. The school's general route times are approximate examples, not universal onset promises or reasons to switch an indicated emergency drug arbitrarily.
肌肉及皮下途径依赖组织吸收和制剂。学校概括的途径时间只是近似例子，不是普遍起效保证，也不能据此任意更换有适应证急救药途径。

00:06:01.008 --> 00:06:14.640
Inhaled bronchodilator delivery often aims at airway smooth muscle rather than requiring all medication to reach an alveolar-capillary surface. The patient's technique and device can change the delivered dose.
吸入支气管扩张药往往作用于气道平滑肌，不要求所有药先到肺泡毛细血管面。患者技术和装置会改变实际到达剂量。

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:29.520
Oral delivery can be appropriate when swallowing is safe and the clinical goal allows its course. An unconscious or vomiting patient may not safely receive an oral medication; speed does not outrank aspiration risk.
安全吞咽且临床目标容许相应时间时，口服可适合。无意识或呕吐者可能不能安全口服；速度不能凌驾误吸风险。

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:45.000
Blood carries drug to tissues. Poor cardiac output or regional perfusion can delay effect even after direct vascular delivery. A poorly perfused target cannot be treated as if drug arrival were guaranteed instantly.
血液将药带到组织。心排量或区域灌注差时，即使直接入血，作用仍会延迟。靶部位灌注差时不能假定药瞬间必到。

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:58.872
The apparent volume of distribution relates the amount of drug in the body to its measured plasma concentration. Extensive tissue uptake can produce a large calculated value, sometimes greater than actual body water.
表观分布容积将体内药物总量与所测血浆浓度联系。组织摄取广泛时计算值可很大，甚至超过真实体水量。

00:06:58.872 --> 00:07:11.232
A larger volume of distribution is not a claim that a new physical tank exists. Lipid solubility, tissue binding, plasma binding and physiological barriers all contribute.
较大分布容积不是说体内有一个新的实体水箱。脂溶性、组织结合、血浆结合和生理屏障都参与。

00:07:11.232 --> 00:07:24.360
The blood-brain and placental barriers are selective, not complete shields. Do not infer that a drug cannot affect the brain or fetus merely because a simple solubility label seems reassuring.
血脑及胎盘屏障具有选择性，却不是完整防护罩。不能只凭简单溶解性标签令人放心，就推断药物不能影响脑或胎儿。

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:37.992
Many medications bind reversibly to plasma proteins such as albumin. The unbound fraction is available to cross membranes and interact with targets; bound drug can act as a reservoir as the balance changes.
许多药与白蛋白等血浆蛋白可逆结合。游离部分可过膜并与靶点相互作用；平衡变化时结合药可起储库作用。

00:07:37.992 --> 00:07:53.544
Low albumin or competition for binding can change the free fraction. Clinical exposure also depends on distribution and clearance, so a changed fraction does not mean every drug's free concentration rises by the same fixed amount.
白蛋白低或结合竞争可改变游离比例。临床暴露还依赖分布和清除，所以比例变化不代表每药游离浓度都固定升同样多。

00:07:53.544 --> 00:08:06.816
Record relevant liver or kidney disease, frailty, recent drugs and the response to previous doses. The safest adjustment is drug-specific and guideline-based, with consultation when indicated.
记录相关肝肾病、衰弱、近期药物及前剂反应。最安全调整按具体药物及指南，适用时会诊。

00:08:06.816 --> 00:08:19.872
Do not copy the school's blanket instruction to always reduce every dose in liver disease. Some drugs are contraindicated, some need adjusted dosing and others require a different decision altogether.
不要照搬学校“肝病所有药剂量一律减少”的笼统说法。有些药禁用，有些需调整，还有些需要完全不同决策。

00:08:19.872 --> 00:08:32.160
Biotransformation chemically changes a drug. The liver is important, but metabolism is not exclusively hepatic and not every reaction follows a strict Phase One then Phase Two sequence.
生物转化以化学方式改变药物。肝很重要，但代谢不只在肝，也不是每个反应都严格先一期再二期。

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:45.360
Phase One includes oxidation, reduction and hydrolysis. Many reactions involve cytochrome enzymes. Phase Two adds a group through conjugation, often helping elimination.
一期包括氧化、还原和水解，许多反应涉及细胞色素酶；二期经结合加上基团，常有助消除。

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:58.848
Metabolism does not always switch the drug off. A prodrug may need activation, and an active metabolite may contribute to benefit or toxicity. Phase Two products are not universally inactive.
代谢并不总把药关闭。前药可能需活化，活性代谢物可能参与疗效或毒性。二期产物也不全是无活性。

00:08:58.848 --> 00:09:12.096
Reduced organ function, low perfusion and enzyme interactions may prolong an effect or reduce activation. Use the actual medication guidance rather than predicting one direction for every drug.
器官功能降低、低灌注及酶相互作用可能延长作用，也可能减少活化。应采用具体药指导，不能为所有药预测同一方向。

00:09:12.096 --> 00:09:22.560
Clearance describes an equivalent volume of plasma cleared of drug per unit time. It is not the actual volume of urine produced, and it is not the half-life.
清除率描述单位时间内相当于被清除药物的血浆体积。它不是实际尿量，也不是半衰期。

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:35.712
Kidneys can remove drug or metabolites through filtration and secretion, with reabsorption influencing the net result. Other drugs depend more on hepatic metabolism, bile or other pathways.
肾可经滤过及分泌排除药物或代谢物，重吸收影响净结果。其他药更依赖肝代谢、胆汁或别的路径。

00:09:35.712 --> 00:09:48.480
If removal is reduced while doses continue, drug or active metabolite can accumulate. A repeat dose must consider the previous doses and elapsed time, not just the current symptom score.
持续给药而排除下降时，药或活性代谢物可蓄积。重复给药须考虑前剂及经过时间，不能只看当前症状分。

00:09:48.480 --> 00:10:01.512
Some renal harms arise from how a drug affects kidney physiology, not merely from poor drug clearance. An NSAID risk assessment therefore includes renal function, perfusion and bleeding context.
有些肾损害来自药物对肾生理的影响，不只是药清不掉。因此NSAID风险评估包括肾功能、灌注和出血背景。

00:10:01.512 --> 00:10:16.968
In a simplified first-order example, one half-life leaves half the amount, two leave one quarter and four leave one sixteenth. Four or five half-lives is substantial reduction, not mathematically complete removal.
简化一级动力学例子中，一半衰期剩一半，两次剩四分之一，四次剩十六分之一。四五个半衰期是大量减少，不是数学上完全清除。

00:10:16.968 --> 00:10:29.952
If an illustrative dose is eighty units, the amounts after successive half-lives are forty, twenty, ten and five. These units are fictional and do not establish a redosing schedule.
假设剂量80单位，连续半衰期后为40、20、10和5。这些是虚构单位，不能据此设重复给药时间。

00:10:29.952 --> 00:10:43.416
Zero-order elimination removes approximately a constant amount in a given time over the relevant concentration range. Saturable handling can make accumulation less predictable than a simple halving rule.
零级消除在相关浓度范围内、给定时间大致排除固定量。处理能力饱和可使蓄积不像简单减半规则那样可预测。

00:10:43.416 --> 00:10:56.400
Clinical effect may outlast a plasma level or end before complete elimination. Active metabolites, redistribution and receptor mechanisms make duration more than a half-life calculation.
临床效应可比某血药水平更久，也可在完全消除前结束。活性代谢物、再分布及受体机制使作用持续时间不只是半衰期计算。

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:08.352
Onset is the time until a measurable effect begins. Peak effect is the strongest effect for the outcome being considered. Duration is how long that relevant effect persists.
起效是开始有可测作用所需时间；峰效是所讨论结局的最强作用；持续时间是该相关作用维持多久。

00:11:08.352 --> 00:11:19.872
The highest plasma concentration is called C max. It need not occur at the exact same moment as peak clinical effect, because effect-site arrival and signaling can lag.
最高血浆浓度称Cmax；由于效应部位到达和信号传递可能滞后，它不一定与临床峰效同时。

00:11:19.872 --> 00:11:34.248
A therapeutic window describes a useful exposure range between inadequate effect and unacceptable toxicity. Boundaries differ between patients and outcomes; a wide window does not make administration error harmless.
治疗窗描述作用不足与不可接受毒性之间的有用暴露范围。边界随患者及结局不同，窗宽也不代表给药错误无害。

00:11:34.248 --> 00:11:47.520
Before a repeat dose, ask whether the expected onset and peak have had time to occur, whether the route worked and whether the patient needs another intervention now. Do not wait for a medicine while ventilation is failing.
重复给药前问：预期起效及峰效时间是否已到、途径是否有效，以及患者现在是否需要别的干预。通气正在衰竭时不能只等药。

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:56.592
Pharmacodynamics asks what the drug does to the body. It includes desired effects, adverse effects and how the effect changes with exposure.
药效学问药物怎样作用于身体，包括预期作用、不良作用及作用如何随暴露变化。

00:11:56.592 --> 00:12:09.240
Two patients may receive the same nominal dose yet have different exposure through pharmacokinetics and different sensitivity through pharmacodynamics. Dose alone cannot predict the entire response.
两名患者名义剂量相同，却可因药动学产生不同暴露、因药效学产生不同敏感性。单看剂量不能预测全部反应。

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:22.584
Many drugs act at receptors, but others target enzymes, change physical properties or participate in chemical processes. The school COX example is an enzyme target, not a newly named receptor.
许多药作用于受体，其他药可靶向酶、改变物理性质或参与化学过程。学校COX示例是酶靶点，不是新起名的受体。

00:12:22.584 --> 00:12:34.056
Link the target to the treatment goal and a monitoring plan. A mechanism explanation becomes clinically useful when it predicts both improvement and an early warning of harm.
把靶点连到治疗目标及监测计划。机制能预测改善和早期伤害警讯时，才具有临床用途。

00:12:34.056 --> 00:12:46.872
Affinity describes binding tendency. Efficacy describes the ability to generate a response in the system. Potency compares the amount or concentration needed for a specified response.
亲和力描述结合倾向；效能描述在该系统中产生响应的能力；效价比较产生特定反应所需药量或浓度。

00:12:46.872 --> 00:12:58.392
A drug can bind well and produce little activation, while another produces a larger response. Binding strength alone does not determine maximum effect or clinical suitability.
药可结合得很好却几乎不激活，另一药可能产生更大反应。结合强度本身不能决定最大作用或临床适合度。

00:12:58.392 --> 00:13:10.680
For concentration-response curves, E C fifty is the concentration producing half that curve's maximal response. It is not the same statement as a dose effective in fifty percent of people.
浓度反应曲线上，EC50是产生该曲线最大反应一半的浓度；它不等于“使一半人有效的剂量”。

00:13:10.680 --> 00:13:21.744
Compare like outcomes under comparable conditions. Potency rankings across different routes, drugs or endpoints are not instructions to exchange equal milligram amounts.
应在可比条件下比较同类结局。不同途径、药物或终点的效价排序，不代表可以按相同毫克互换。

00:13:21.744 --> 00:13:34.128
On the schematic, A reaches a specified submaximal response at a lower concentration than B. That shows greater potency for the illustrated response, not a larger maximum.
示意图中，A以比B更低浓度达到某指定次最大反应，显示针对该反应效价更高，不是最大作用更大。

00:13:34.128 --> 00:13:45.624
C reaches a lower maximum in this model. Its curve cannot be made into A simply by moving further right. Maximal response and concentration needed are separate features.
C在本模型达到较低最大值。不能只继续向右加量就让它变成A。最大反应与所需浓度是分开特征。

00:13:45.624 --> 00:13:57.336
Once useful response plateaus, additional drug may increase another unwanted effect. A ceiling on one outcome does not guarantee a ceiling on every toxicity.
有用反应平台后，再加药可能增加另一不良作用。某结局有天花板，不代表所有毒性都有天花板。

00:13:57.336 --> 00:14:06.552
These original curves have no clinical dose scale. Practise explaining their shapes, then use the actual drug monograph for safe patient dosing.
这些原创曲线没有临床剂量刻度。练习解释形状后，患者安全剂量仍用真实药物专论。

00:14:06.552 --> 00:14:18.240
An agonist activates a receptor. A full agonist can produce the reference maximal response in a particular system, while a partial agonist has a lower maximal response there.
激动剂激活受体。完全激动剂可在特定系统产生参照最大反应，部分激动剂在该处最大反应较低。

00:14:18.240 --> 00:14:29.952
Morphine is the school's full opioid-agonist example and buprenorphine the partial-agonist example. These are mechanism comparisons, not permission for routine PCP administration.
学校以吗啡作完全阿片激动剂、丁丙诺啡作部分激动剂示例。这是机制比较，不授权PCP常规使用。

00:14:29.952 --> 00:14:43.728
A partial agonist may compete with a full agonist and reduce the response. In an opioid-dependent patient, certain transitions can precipitate withdrawal; the clinical plan must use the applicable protocol.
部分激动剂可与完全激动剂竞争并降低反应。阿片依赖患者在某些转换时会诱发戒断，临床计划须使用适用流程。

00:14:43.728 --> 00:14:56.112
Do not infer that a partial agonist cannot cause serious respiratory depression, especially with other depressants. The school's ceiling-effect language is not a guarantee of harmless overdose.
不能推断部分激动剂不会造成严重呼吸抑制，尤其合并其他抑制物。学校的天花板作用表述不保证过量无害。

00:14:56.112 --> 00:15:09.912
A competitive antagonist competes with an agonist for binding at the receptor. In an ideal experimental model, enough agonist can overcome the blockade; this is not permission to give an unsafe clinical dose.
竞争性拮抗剂与激动剂竞争受体结合。理想实验模型中足够激动剂可克服阻断，但这不允许临床给予不安全剂量。

00:15:09.912 --> 00:15:22.656
Noncompetitive mechanisms reduce response in a way that additional agonist cannot simply reverse. Describe the actual target rather than using antagonist as a loose name for every inhibitor.
非竞争机制以额外激动剂不能简单逆转的方式降低响应。应描述真实靶点，不能把任何抑制剂都笼统叫受体拮抗剂。

00:15:22.656 --> 00:15:36.816
Naloxone blocks opioid receptor effects. Reversal can restore ventilation, but the opioid may last longer and non-opioid causes may coexist. Continue airway support and reassessment.
纳洛酮阻断阿片受体作用。逆转可能恢复通气，但阿片可更持久，也可能合并非阿片病因。继续气道支持和复评。

00:15:36.816 --> 00:15:55.656
Organophosphates inhibit acetylcholinesterase, allowing acetylcholine to accumulate. The school calls them an irreversible agonist in one passage; that is not a direct receptor mechanism. Atropine blocks muscarinic effects but does not repair every toxic effect.
有机磷抑制乙酰胆碱酯酶，使乙酰胆碱积聚。学校某段称其不可逆激动剂，那不是直接受体机制。阿托品阻断毒蕈碱作用，但不能修复全部毒性。

00:15:55.656 --> 00:16:09.336
Opioid receptor activation can reduce pain, but also lower respiratory drive and awareness. Miosis, nausea, reduced gut activity and circulatory effects may accompany the response.
阿片受体激活可减轻痛，也会降低呼吸驱动和意识。可能同时出现瞳孔缩小、恶心、肠活动减少及循环作用。

00:16:09.336 --> 00:16:22.200
Assess respiratory rate together with depth, air movement, airway protection and mental status. A displayed saturation on oxygen can remain reassuring while ventilation worsens.
呼吸频率要连同深度、气流、气道保护和意识评估。给氧时显示血氧可能仍好看，但通气正在恶化。

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:35.040
An opioid toxidrome is a pattern, not a requirement that every sign be present. Do not withhold ventilation because pupils are not pinpoint or because the exact substance is unknown.
阿片中毒综合征是模式，不要求每项征象都齐。不能因瞳孔不针尖或不知准确物质而不支持通气。

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:48.984
Naloxone may improve opioid-related ventilation, but recurrence and withdrawal are possible. Use the actual dosing pathway and continue reassessment rather than declaring the patient cured after awakening.
纳洛酮可改善阿片相关通气，但可能复发或戒断。按真实剂量路径继续复评，不能醒来就宣布治愈。

00:16:48.984 --> 00:17:02.328
Alpha one activation generally increases vascular tone. Beta one effects include increased heart rate, contractility and conduction. Beta two activation relaxes bronchial smooth muscle.
α1激活通常增加血管张力；β1作用包括增加心率、收缩力和传导；β2激活舒张支气管平滑肌。

00:17:02.328 --> 00:17:16.608
Epinephrine acts across alpha and beta systems. That helps explain its role in anaphylaxis, where airway, breathing and circulation can all be threatened. Route and dose remain indication-specific.
肾上腺素作用于α及β系统，帮助解释其在气道、呼吸和循环均可能受威胁的过敏反应中的作用。途径及剂量仍随适应证不同。

00:17:16.608 --> 00:17:29.136
Salbutamol preferentially targets beta two receptors, but selectivity is not absolute. Reassess airflow and work of breathing as well as tremor, heart rate and other adverse effects.
沙丁胺醇优先作用β2，但选择性非绝对。应重查进气和呼吸功，也看震颤、心率及其他不良作用。

00:17:29.136 --> 00:17:41.904
A faster pulse after a bronchodilator does not by itself prove treatment failure or success. Compare breathing, perfusion, patient experience and the time course before deciding what to do next.
扩张药后心率更快，不能独自证明失败或成功。下一步决策前，应比较呼吸、灌注、患者感受和时间过程。

00:17:41.904 --> 00:17:55.104
Muscarinic receptor activity can increase secretions, constrict bronchi, slow the heart and increase gastrointestinal activity. Effects depend on the receptor location and physiological context.
毒蕈碱受体活动可增加分泌、收缩支气管、减慢心率并增加胃肠活动。具体作用依部位及生理背景不同。

00:17:55.104 --> 00:18:10.920
The school mnemonic SLUDGEM lists salivation, lacrimation, urination, defecation, gastrointestinal upset, emesis and miosis. Its three Bs highlight bronchorrhea, bronchospasm and bradycardia.
学校SLUDGEM列流涎、流泪、排尿、排便、胃肠不适、呕吐和瞳孔缩小；三个B强调支气管大量分泌、痉挛及心动过缓。

00:18:10.920 --> 00:18:25.176
Atropine and ipratropium block muscarinic actions in different indications. A cholinergic poisoning can also affect nicotinic and central pathways, so atropine is not a complete cure for every manifestation.
阿托品和异丙托溴铵在不同适应证阻断毒蕈碱作用。胆碱能中毒也可影响烟碱及中枢途径，因此阿托品不是所有表现的完整解药。

00:18:25.176 --> 00:18:40.176
Do not enter a contaminated area to administer an antidote without the required protection. Scene safety, appropriate decontamination, ventilation and specialist support are part of the treatment, not optional extras.
未有必需防护，不能为给解毒剂就进入污染区。现场安全、适当去污、通气及专门支援本就是治疗一部分，不是可选附加。

00:18:40.176 --> 00:18:55.824
H one signaling contributes to itch, vascular changes and allergic manifestations. H two signaling includes gastric acid secretion. The shared word histamine does not make the receptors or treatments interchangeable.
H1信号参与瘙痒、血管变化和过敏表现；H2信号包括胃酸分泌。同为组胺，不使受体及治疗可互换。

00:18:55.824 --> 00:19:09.672
First-generation H one medicines may cause sedation and anticholinergic effects. Dimenhydrinate and diphenhydramine share some pharmacology, but their indications and authorization are not identical.
第一代H1药可能镇静并产生抗胆碱作用。茶苯海明与苯海拉明部分药理相似，但适应证和授权不同。

00:19:09.672 --> 00:19:24.024
Life-threatening anaphylaxis needs epinephrine and airway, breathing and circulation care. Relief of itch does not correct shock or dangerous airway swelling, and an antihistamine must not delay epinephrine.
危及生命的全身过敏需要肾上腺素及ABC照护。止痒不能纠正休克或危险气道肿胀，抗组胺不能延误肾上腺素。

00:19:24.024 --> 00:19:37.272
Do not decide that a reaction is harmless merely because a non-IgE mechanism is suspected. Judge physiological compromise; immune and non-immune mechanisms can produce serious systemic reactions.
不能只因怀疑非IgE机制，就认定反应无害。应判断生理受损；免疫及非免疫机制都可能产生严重全身反应。

00:19:37.272 --> 00:19:49.848
The school uses the serotonin receptor five H T three to connect gut and central emesis pathways. Ondansetron blocks that receptor and can reduce nausea and vomiting.
学校用血清素5-HT3受体联系胃肠及中枢呕吐途径。昂丹司琼阻断该受体，可减少恶心呕吐。

00:19:49.848 --> 00:20:02.112
This is different from the vestibular and anticholinergic effects emphasized for dimenhydrinate. Similar symptom goals do not imply identical mechanisms, doses or eligibility.
这与茶苯海明强调的前庭及抗胆碱作用不同。症状目标相似，不代表机制、剂量或资格相同。

00:20:02.112 --> 00:20:17.808
Before treating the symptom, assess its context: onset, pain, neurological findings, perfusion, pregnancy possibility, ingestion and relevant history. Nausea may accompany an important underlying emergency.
治疗症状前先评估背景：起病、疼痛、神经发现、灌注、妊娠可能、摄入物及相关病史。恶心可能伴重要急症。

00:20:17.808 --> 00:20:30.360
After an authorized antiemetic, reassess symptom response, safety and the underlying problem. A patient who stops vomiting has not necessarily become safe to leave or delay.
使用获授权止吐药后，重查症状反应、安全及潜在问题。停止呕吐不代表已安全到可留下或延误。

00:20:30.360 --> 00:20:42.072
Cyclooxygenase enzymes support prostaglandin and thromboxane pathways. These affect pain, inflammation, fever, vascular physiology and platelet activity.
环氧合酶支持前列腺素及血栓素途径，影响痛、炎症、发热、血管生理和血小板活动。

00:20:42.072 --> 00:20:54.192
ASA irreversibly inhibits platelet cyclooxygenase and reduces thromboxane-mediated aggregation for the affected platelet's lifespan. It does not directly dissolve an existing clot.
ASA不可逆抑制血小板环氧合酶，在受影响血小板寿命内减少血栓素介导聚集，但不直接溶解现有血栓。

00:20:54.192 --> 00:21:07.152
Ibuprofen and ketorolac are other COX-inhibiting medicines with analgesic benefits and renal, gastrointestinal and bleeding risks. They cannot simply substitute for ASA's acute-coronary role.
布洛芬及酮咯酸也是抑制COX药，既有镇痛益处，也有肾、胃肠及出血风险，不能简单替代ASA在急性冠脉中的作用。

00:21:07.152 --> 00:21:21.336
The school briefly describes ASA as binding platelet receptors. The more precise target here is an enzyme. Match the actual mechanism to the indication, and check the specific contraindications.
学校某处把ASA写成结合血小板受体；这里更准确的靶点是酶。应把真实机制与适应证联系，并查具体禁忌。

00:21:21.336 --> 00:21:37.032
An adult has reduced awareness and inadequate slow breathing. A bystander reports an unknown tablet. Start the immediate assessment and support airway and ventilation; do not wait to identify the receptor before treating failure.
成人意识下降、呼吸缓慢不足，旁人说吃了未知片剂。先做即时评估并支持气道通气，不能等确认受体才处理衰竭。

00:21:37.032 --> 00:21:49.056
If an opioid contribution is suspected and naloxone is indicated and authorized, use the actual pathway. Name the goal as improved functional ventilation, then monitor the result.
若怀疑阿片参与且纳洛酮有适应证、获授权，应采用实际路径。目标说成改善功能通气，再监测结果。

00:21:49.056 --> 00:22:01.176
No immediate change can reflect delivery, onset, dose or a different or mixed cause. Automatic repeated doses without those checks can waste time and create harm.
未立即改善可能与给药、起效、剂量或不同混合病因有关。不核查就机械重复给药，可能浪费时间并造成伤害。

00:22:01.176 --> 00:22:14.544
An initial improvement followed by decline can reflect a longer-acting opioid or another problem. PK predicts recurrence risk, PD explains the reversal, and assessment decides the next safe action.
先改善后下降可能是阿片更长效或另有问题。药动学预测复发风险，药效学解释逆转，而评估决定下一安全行动。

00:22:14.544 --> 00:22:26.784
Without notes, distinguish dose from concentration and pharmacokinetics from pharmacodynamics. Explain why immediate blood entry does not guarantee immediate peak effect.
不看笔记区分剂量和浓度、药动学和药效学，并解释为何立即入血不保证立即峰效。

00:22:26.784 --> 00:22:36.960
Sketch the half-life sequence and compare potency with maximal response. Then explain why the sketch cannot tell you an actual patient's safe dose.
画半衰期序列，比较效价和最大反应，再解释为什么图不能告诉你真实患者安全剂量。

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:49.992
For opioid, adrenergic, muscarinic, histamine, serotonin and COX targets, give an intended effect and one important harm or limitation. Say what you would reassess.
对阿片、肾上腺素能、毒蕈碱、组胺、血清素及COX靶点，各说一个预期作用和重要伤害或局限，并说复评什么。

00:22:49.992 --> 00:23:03.552
Next, apply these mechanisms to the school's medication-safety, adult monograph, pediatric calculation and scope sections. Correct science is necessary, but it is not the complete authorization decision.
接着把这些机制应用到学校药物安全、成人专论、儿科计算及权限分节。科学正确必需，但不是完整授权决策。
